license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Data, instruments, prompts and scripts for a study of the evidence on which
  human-in-the-loop arrangements for delegating deductive coding to language
  models rest. The package contains 113 reference claims and their 31-code
  taxonomy, five blind human coding sheets, two escalation-round sheets with
  every instrument as sent, and 20,340 decisions from three language models
  under scaffolded and unscaffolded conditions. A single script recomputes 110
  quantities reported in the accompanying article and checks each against
  the value printed there.
keywords:
  - human-AI collaboration
  - authority allocation
  - large language models
  - deductive coding
  - evidence synthesis
  - inter-rater reliability
  - empirical software engineering
  - replication package
